{
	"_readme": [
		"The same game played BADLY, on purpose, because a driver that plays well only ever visits",
		"the branches good play reaches. Nothing here is a fixture: it is the shipped quest, lost.",
		"",
		"press_until_state mashes, and only the FIRST press of a cue is captured - so a masher's",
		"press always lands early and never scores. That is what makes this a bad driver for free,",
		"and it is why the Keeper kills them: four unblocked hits against twenty-four health.",
		"",
		"What only this script ever reaches: fleeing a fight and finding it still standing, a boss",
		"refusing to be fled, losing, the game-over screen, and the road back from it."
	],
	"steps": [
		{
			"op": "note",
			"text": "the title opens the game now. A --qa-script run points saves at user://qa_saves and empties it at boot, so there is never anything to Continue - and the cursor opens on the row a press will actually do something with, which is New game. Rows: Continue, New game. One press starts the run."
		},
		{
			"op": "assert_state",
			"state": "title"
		},
		{
			"op": "press",
			"action": "interact"
		},
